cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MicroCLIP or MicroPool-2M in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "MicroCLIP: Connecting Text and Microscopy Images via Contrastive Language-Image Pretraining"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "TODO(release): repository URL"
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - vision-language pretraining
  - contrastive learning
  - zero-shot classification
  - image-text retrieval
authors:
  - name: "TODO(release): the MicroCLIP authors"
abstract: >-
  MicroCLIP is a 150M-parameter vision-language model for single-channel fluorescence
  microscopy, fine-tuned from DFN2B-CLIP ViT-B/16 on MicroPool-2M, a 2.5M-image corpus
  annotated with category titles, per-image descriptions, and knowledge-level biological
  captions. The released checkpoint reaches 98.46% zero-shot Top-1 in domain and retains
  67.70% / 34.07% / 46.13% under compositional, cell-line, and organelle-set shift, and
  supports cross-modal retrieval at 61.5% I2T / 63.3% T2I Recall@1.
